{{!< default}}
{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>Author &mdash; The Faith Received</title>
<meta name="description" content="An author in The Faith Received: their dates, tradition, a short life, the scripture they quoted most, and every work of theirs the library holds." />
<meta property="og:title" content="Author — The Faith Received" />
<meta property="og:description" content="An author in The Faith Received: their dates, tradition, a short life, the scripture they quoted most, and every work of theirs the library holds." />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="Author — The Faith Received" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="An author in The Faith Received: their dates, tradition, a short life, the scripture they quoted most, and every work of theirs the library holds." />
{{/contentFor}}
{{!-- /the-faith-received/author/?a=<folded-name>

     One page per author, rendered at read time by faith-author.js.
     There are well over fourteen thousand names across the seven
     collections and they change whenever the source republishes, so
     generating a template each is not the shape of this problem.

     Built on the room hero so an author reads as a place in the
     library rather than as a search result. --}}

<main class="faith-received faith-author-page">

  <section class="bhero bhero--tool bhero--author">
    <div class="bhero-inner container">
      <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="/the-faith-received/browse/">Author</a></p>
      <h1 data-faith-author-name>Loading&hellip;</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bband faith-author-body">
    <div class="container" data-faith-author data-fr-bookmark-rows>
      <p class="faith-author-empty">Loading&hellip;</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{!-- Positions was here: "what this writer is recorded as holding,
       doctrine by doctrine", a doctrine picker over the mined statement
       set. Removed from the author page on Ian's instruction,
       2026-09-11.

       The reason it could not stay is the standing rule that the
       library quotes and never paraphrases. Every statement in that
       data is a paraphrase — the mined set carries no verbatim text
       anywhere — and the panel said so itself, in a standing caveat
       telling the reader to go and check the passage before
       attributing any of it to the author. A feature that has to warn
       you not to trust it is not one this library should be running.

       The data and faith-positions.js are untouched and still serve
       /the-faith-received/doctrines/ and the topic pages. Only the
       author-page mount is gone. --}}

  {{!-- BETA GATE. The life and the shelf are open to everyone: an
       author page is the library's own catalogue and a reader who
       cannot yet see it has nothing to sign in for. The research
       panels are the gated part, and they are gated by NOT LOADING
       THEIR SCRIPTS at the foot of this page, inside a
       {{#if @member}}. Nothing draws them, so there is no markup to
       hide and no flash to avoid. That is the server gate the contract
       in partials/faith-received/_beta-gate.hbs asks for, in the only
       shape a page whose body is built by JS can take it.

       "Account" here means ANY signed-in Ghost member, free included. --}}
  {{> "faith-received/_beta-gate"}}

{{> "faith-received/_beta-band"}}
</main>
{{!-- Sitewide membership CTA. The partial's own rule is "hide for paid
     and comped"; during the beta this page wants it hidden for every
     signed-in member, free included, because a free member is using
     the research panels above right now. Same wrapper and same
     reasoning as /the-faith-received/ask/ and /search/. --}}
<div data-tfr-gate="signed-out">{{> "faith-received/_library-cta"}}</div>



<meta name="tfr-library-base" content="https://mo-tfr-library.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev" />
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-corpora.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-century.js"}}"></script>

{{!-- ── The research panels, member-only for the beta ──────────────
     Search this author, the scripture fingerprint, reception and the
     topic index. All four are drawn by these scripts into
     [data-faith-author] at read time, so not loading them IS the
     server gate: a signed-out visitor is served no panel markup, no
     panel CSS state and no fetch, and the beta-gate box above stands
     where they would have been.

     faith-author.js below asks for each of these with a
     `window.MO…` guard and draws the life and the shelf without any
     of them, which is what makes this branch safe to take. Do not
     move faith-author.js inside it.

     ORDER MATTERS in one place only: faith-author-panels.js defines
     the fold the other three build into, so it goes first. --}}
{{#if @member}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-author-panels.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- Search this author. Power Search is the first mode and the one
     the box opens on: the same semantic search as the Research desk,
     with the library narrowed to this author's own works. The two
     older modes stay beside it, and the scripture one is load-bearing
     rather than legacy: the fingerprint's verse figures call
     MOAuthorSearch.find() and answer inside this panel.

     faith-text.js is the one way to get the text of a work whatever
     collection it is in; faith-corpus-search.js is Find over a set of
     them, which is what the word-or-phrase mode walks. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-text.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-corpus-search.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-author-power.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-author-search.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- The scripture fingerprint: what this author quoted, from the
     generated index, drawn above the search panel and driving it. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-author-scripture.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- Reception: who else in the library cites this author, and who
     this author cites in turn. Draws beside the fingerprint, both
     fetched once faith-author.js has resolved the author's name. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-author-reception.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- The topic index: the same mined topics the Compare desk offers,
     for this one author, with the count of recorded statements and
     the works they sit in. Counts and links only. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-author-topics.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- The submit button in the search panel carries
     data-feature-gate="ask". Today that tier is "any signed-in
     member" and the modal never fires; when the beta ends it becomes
     member-tier and this is the only thing that tells a free
     subscriber why the search did nothing. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/feature-gate.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- faith-positions.js is not loaded here any more; see the note where
     its band used to be. It still runs on the doctrines and topic
     pages. --}}
{{/if}}

<script src="{{asset "js/faith-author.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- Bookmark a work from its row. The store first: it is the same
     mo-kit bookmark the reader's Save button and the Bookmark button at
     the foot of a section write, so a work saved here and a section
     saved inside it are one record, not two. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/lib/faith-work-bookmarks.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-work-bookmark-rows.js"}}"></script>

{{!-- Claims the TFR / TFR-Beta Kit tags for a signed-in member. Hides
     and reveals nothing; see the file header. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-beta-gate.js"}}"></script>
